# The plugin library.
#
# Chosen for live sound on a digital console, not for studio production: the
# question asked of each entry was "would a system tech reach for this during a
# service", and instruments, samplers and synthesisers are therefore absent.
# docs/PLUGINS.md lists the extras, and how to add them in one command.
#
# Everything here is free software from the Ubuntu archive - GPL, LGPL or
# MIT - which means it is redistributable inside an ISO, and updated by the same
# `apt upgrade` as the rest of the machine. That constraint is the reason a few
# well-regarded plugins are missing rather than an oversight; see docs/PLUGINS.md.

# --- Linux Studio Plugins ------------------------------------------------------
# The centrepiece. Parametric EQ up to 32 bands, compressor, sidechain
# compressor, expander, gate, limiter, de-esser, crossover, delay compensator,
# impulse-response loader, loudness and spectrum analysis. Consistently the
# highest-rated free suite on Linux, and unusual in shipping VST3 as well as LV2,
# so the same plugin loads whichever format you reach for.
lsp-plugins-lv2
lsp-plugins-vst3

# --- Calf Studio Gear ----------------------------------------------------------
# Compressor, multiband compressor, sidechain gate, EQ (5/8/12/30 band), reverb,
# exciter, bass enhancer, vintage delay, analyzer. Very legible interfaces, which
# matters when someone else has to drive the rig.
calf-plugins

# --- x42 / Robin Gareus ---------------------------------------------------------
# fil4 EQ, digital peak limiter with true-peak detection, a-comp, a-exp, a-delay,
# and the meter set that makes a broadcast or streamed service straightforward:
# EBU R128 loudness, K-meters, true-peak, phase correlation, goniometer. Also
# tuna, a tuner accurate enough for a line check.
x42-plugins

# --- ZamAudio -------------------------------------------------------------------
# ZamComp, ZamCompX2, ZamEQ2, ZamGate, ZaMaximX2, ZamGEQ31, ZamTube, ZamDelay.
# Small, fast, and the 31-band graphic is the familiar shape for ringing out a
# room by hand when you want to do it the old way.
zam-plugins

# --- Reverb ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# DragonFly: hall, room, plate and early-reflection algorithms. The best free
# reverb on the platform by common consent.
dragonfly-reverb
# Fons Adriaensen's zita-rev1 and zita-at1 are deliberately NOT here. They are
# excellent, and they are standalone JACK applications rather than plugins - they
# install binaries, not .lv2 bundles, so the host cannot instantiate them and
# listing them here would inflate the plugin count with things that are not
# plugins. docs/PLUGINS.md says how to add them and how to use them.

# --- Further channel-strip and utility sets -------------------------------------
# eq10q: parametric EQ, compressor, gate, bass enhancer.
eq10q
# Invada: compressor, delay, filters, tube distortion, meters.
invada-studio-plugins-lv2
# abGate: a clean, low-CPU noise gate.
abgate
# Fons Adriaensen's plugins as LV2 - parametric EQ, phaser, chorus.
fomp
# MDA: the classic free set, ported to LV2.
mda-lv2
# TAP: reverberator, dynamics, echo. Old, still good, almost free CPU-wise.
tap-plugins
# CAPS: plate reverb, compressor, EQ, amp models.
caps
# SWH: the LADSPA collection most other free plugins were measured against.
swh-plugins

# --- Guitar and instrument amplification ------------------------------------------
# guitarix supplies amp and cabinet models plus a large effects set as LV2, which
# is what turns a DI'd guitar into something that sits in a mix without a physical
# amp on stage.
guitarix-lv2
